From 70a6ee7c63bcda9bacc640fec27570cafbbb1af3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 01:11:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(post): keep the .mch part tree as MachineTree

parse_mch flattens kinematics.default.parts into Machine.axes and drops
the parent chain. A machine model needs the chain.

parse_mch_tree reads the same JSON into a MachineTree: each part with its
id, name, type, parent index and stated facts (travel, axis, pivot,
offset, direction, spindle body, tool station), in mm. An axis that is an
ancestor of a head part is on the tool side; each other axis is on the
table side. A malformed tree refuses with the part id and the key.

Machine, parse_mch and the existing checks do not change. rate, scale and
mm_factor of parse.rs are now pub(super), so the two readers share one
unit and unstated-limit law.

Fixes #2583

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
